workedExamples.question_text:
The graph shows $\log_{10}N$ against time, where $N$ is a culture's population. By what factor does the population increase over the four hours shown?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=12mm,y=10mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{mathblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[draw=black,->] (0,0)--(4.6,0) node[right] {$t$ (hours)};
\draw[draw=black,->] (0,0)--(0,4.6) node[above] {$\log_{10}N$};
\foreach \x in {0,1,2,3,4} {\draw[draw=black] (\x,0.07)--(\x,-0.07);\path (\x,-0.07) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\x$};}
\foreach \y in {1,2,3,4} {\draw[draw=black] (0.07,\y)--(-0.07,\y);\path (-0.07,\y) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\y$};}
\draw[draw=mathblue,thick] (0,2)--(4,4);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

