The graph plots $\log_{10}N$ against time for a bacterial culture, where $N$ is the number of bacteria.
By what factor does the culture grow over the $6$ hours shown?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[width=8.5cm,height=7cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=-0.3,xmax=7,ymin=0,ymax=6.6,xtick={0,1,...,6},ytick={0,1,...,6},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\small,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={$t$ (hours)},ylabel={$\log_{10}N$},ylabel near ticks]
\addplot[thick,blue!70!black,domain=0:6,samples=2] {2+0.5*x};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
